    "text": "Thursday, February 12, 2026\nLiam Chapman, 7, foreground, builds a fort in the snow Sunday in his yard on Lincoln Street. His sister, Abby, 9, was building a snowman. Nearly 1.5 feet of snow already has fallen in Jamestown, which is more than the entire 2024-25 winter. PHOTOS BY ANDREA VON HOHENLEITEN\nCalvin Byers, 4, tosses a snowball Sunday at his dad, Stan, in the parking lot at St. Matthew’s Episcopal Church.\nDean Jennings uses a snow blower Saturday to clear Rainbow Pond as his son, Grant Jennings, 12, helps with a shovel.",
